{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4a896caa-515b-4714-8f62-3c7639fb8c47",
    "name": "ImageShield services — control-room API",
    "description": "Control-room API of the ImageShield **services** (image_flashbacklabs) — the surface the shipped console (`console/`, port 8082) is built on, and the contract an admin panel needs. 22 requests.\n\n## Auth — two machine tokens on every admin request\n- `X-Service-Token: {{service_token}}` — required by EVERY services route.\n- `X-Admin-Service-Token: {{admin_service_token}}` — required IN ADDITION on every `/v1/admin/*` route. The two values must differ (services refuse to boot otherwise).\n- Operator identity is DATA, not auth: every write body carries `\"operator\": \"{{operator}}\"`, which lands in `audit_log`. Set `operator` to your real name.\n\nMissing or wrong tokens → `401 {\"error\": {\"code\": \"unauthorised\", ...}}`. Every error uses the envelope `{\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\", \"retryable\", \"request_id\"}}`; `422` adds `error.details` (`loc` + `msg`). Show `request_id` in error toasts — it is the log-correlation handle. Decimals cross as STRINGS.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this collection AND `imageshield-services-dev.postman_environment.json`; select the **ImageShield services — dev** environment.\n2. Fill `service_token` and `admin_service_token` from Secrets Manager (`imageshield/dev/service-token/backend-to-services` → `token`; `imageshield/dev/service-token/admin` → `token`). Never commit them.\n3. `services_base_url`: services sit on a PRIVATE subnet (host port 8081) — nothing external reaches them by design. Two ways in:\n   - **Local stack**: `docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml up -d`, `python scripts/migrate.py up`, `python -m imageshield` → `http://localhost:8081`.\n   - **Dev in AWS**: `aws ssm start-session --target i-0d277703b778392ef --document-name AWS-StartPortForwardingSession --parameters portNumber=8081,localPortNumber=8081` → `http://localhost:8081`.\n4. Run **00 - Health** first: `/v1/ping` proves the service token, `01 → providers/health` proves the admin token.\n\n## For the team building the admin panel — read `docs/ADMIN_PANEL_INTEGRATION.md` first\nRule 0 there: a panel's BROWSER never talks to the services. The backend (image_backend) holds these two tokens and proxies these calls over the private network; the frontend's contract is whatever admin routes the backend exposes on top of this. This collection is therefore the services-side contract those backend routes must mirror — the shapes, codes and rules are the same either way. Rule 5: staff never see hit imagery; `image_url` on a review card is evidence for URL-context review, never something to render, proxy, cache or hotlink.\n\nRequests that create things (`03 → POST threat-events`, `05 → POST articles`) capture the new id into `event_id` / `article_id` so the follow-on requests chain. The example threat event penalises REAL matched scores on whatever environment you point at — retract it afterwards.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 - Health & readiness",
      "description": "Tokenless `/health` and the readiness gate `/readyz`: 503 with named `problems` when the `svc` contract (nine views, their column types, the proxy grant) is broken. `/v1/ping` proves the service token before you debug an admin call.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health — always 200 when the process answers",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{services_base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{services_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No token. DB reachability only. The ECS health-check target."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /readyz — 200 ready, or 503 with problems[]",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{services_base_url}}/readyz",
              "host": [
                "{{services_base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "readyz"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No token. `{status, version, db, problems}`. Expect `problems: []` on a good deploy; a 503 names `missing_view`, `missing_column`, `wrong_column_type`, `missing_select_grant`."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
